  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2017, the ILO undertook an assessment of the Enabling Environment for Sustainable Enterprises (EESE) in Namibia based on a primary enterprise survey and review of secondary data on political, economic, social and environmental indicators. The EESE assessment confirmed the lack of an enabling business environment and especially the lack of access to financial and non-financial business development services (BDS) are the key constraints to entrepreneurship and sustainable enterprises development. 

NEF Launched the EESE report and a Private sector Business Agenda. The Business Agenda (BA) proposes specific reforms to be implemented for improved business environment in Namibia 

The ILO trained employers on convention 111 including other related areas as identified by CAS. In 2022, the ILO delivered two trainings on C11 focusing on: 
a) Strengthened knowledge base on ILS, including those related to gender equality and HIV /AIDS. 
b) Employers sensitized on Convention 111 and related recommendations as per CAS 
c) Highlight the case for and the benefits of implementing the convention 
d) Sharing best practice on implementing the convention 
e) Employers guided to identify and document: 
Immediate actions they need to take in aligning their policies with C111 
A roadmap for further capacity building on C111 and other equality conventions and Recommendations 
Action plan (with time frame) to develop an industry self-regulation system/mechanism 

The Namibia Employers Federation (NEF)  strategic plan for 2017-2019  long expired  and there will be need for NEF  to relook at the new environment vs its current capacity and to articulate a roadmap for delivering its mandate in the next 3-5 years. Further, the changing business environment at the national, regional, and global levels, particularly the effects of COVID-19 pandemic call for the NEF to reflect on its strategic focus, assess the risks it may face in the future with a view to align its efforts with</narrative>
  </description>
